{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1221347-help-with-siberian-cofd-game","id":1221347,"title":"Help with Siberian CofD game","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-05-22T18:54:03-07:00","id":1221347,"title":"Help with Siberian CofD game","content":"Hello all,<br /> <br /> So I am planning out a siberian chronicle set in post WW2, cold war era Russia and I wanted to give my players a somewhat iconic horror/spirit to start off with. So i did some research and stumbled upon Baba Yaga.<br /> <br /> I was hoping to create a horror or spirit version of her for this chronicle but i am very green at this so did a little aearching and stumbled upon this post:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1208030-horrors-from-mythologies?p=1210005#post1210005\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1208030-horrors-from-mythologies?p=1210005#post1210005\"> Horrors from mythologies - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1208030-horrors-from-mythologies?p=1210005#post1210005\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1208030-horrors-from-mythologies?p=1210005#post1210005 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Inspired by Kinship Horros topic (http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1206121-kinship </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> It however doesnt quite look like a horror template so im guessing it must be something exclusive to beast? Would it be easy enough to make a horror or spirit out of the Baba tale or am i barking up the wrong tree?<br /> <br /> Thanks for the help!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24020-mateus","name":"Mateus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24020_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-22T21:32:13-07:00","id":1221378,"title":"","content":"Baba Yaga! Iron-toothed and ravenous, who flies about with mortar and pestle, who lives in a chicken-footed house. Baba Yaga! Eldest and most terrible, who counts dead men\u2019s fingers and devours those fools who enter her house, who can smell the blood of a Russian man without fail.<br /> <br /> She most definitely has the makings of a Horror, and most likely a potent one indeed. (Remember, too, that she is served by three knights: first there comes a white knight on a white horse, then a red knight on a red horse, lastly a black knight on a black horse.)<br /> <br /> A spirit? Possibly. But everything about Baba Yaga suggests that she is terribly, impossibly physical and present. It\u2019s possible that references to her chicken-legged hut actually mean that those she possesses have their hands warped and crooked into talons; it\u2019s also quite possible that, somewhere out in the woods, there\u2019s a slowly revolving hut on two huge, bloodstained legs, surrounded by a fence of skulls. (She likes to keep them fresh. Some of the skulls are very small indeed.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12958-raz_fox","name":"Raz_Fox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-22T21:54:33-07:00","id":1221379,"title":"","content":"Hm, the only reason I'd hesitate to use Baba Yaga is because of how resonant she is as a mythological entity in the region. She feels like she'd be a super heavy hitter as a spirit or horror. The Slavic region, however, is full of various spirits, fae, monsters and devils. <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Supernatural_beings_in_Slavic_religion\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Supern...lavic_religion</a> could be a good jumping off point. However, if you do want to use Baba Yaga I'd probably have her be diminished somehow (lack of belief in the modern era etc.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","name":"Gullinbursti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5439_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"291"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-23T02:06:56-07:00","id":1221422,"title":"","content":"Or just waking up after a long nap. But, yeah I'd go Potency 8-10 Horror with Immortal as one of her Dread Powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-23T03:23:28-07:00","id":1221431,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Baba Yaga is kinda of a big deal, unless you diminish/limit her powers for a reason of another. Which would be absolutely fine, mind you.<br /> <br /> As for the Dread Powers she might have, those are the ones I'd pick from: Beastmaster, Eye Spy, Home Ground, Hypnotic Gaze, Immortal, Natural Weapons, Madness and Terror, Maze, Miracle, Snare, and Soul-Thief. Give her a flying vehicle in the shape of her mortar and don't forget about her chicken-legged hut and you're good to .<br /> <br /> Should you decide to keep her as a powerful being, might I suggest to make her a more ambiguous NPC, at least at the beginning? Baba Yaga is sinister, almost surely evil and dealing with her is a really dangerous matter, but in myths she often is willing to have a chat and even provide assistance to the protagonist. Depending on the story you have in mind, there are a lot of ways you can use her. Just be sure to not get on her bad side.<br /> <br /> Regardless of the state of her powers, the old lady is a big character in the context of supernatural Russia, so it makes sense for her to have plenty of servants and even more creatures that are scared of her. Little spirits, old enemies, people she cursed and all that comes in between.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 05-23-2018, 06:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-23T15:04:00-07:00","id":1221553,"title":"","content":"Thanks for all the input! This is a great help!<br /> <br /> I read somewhere that in the native tongue of the region, suberia means &quot;sleeping land&quot; and if this chronicle goes long i was thinking of playing that up and &quot;waking&quot; siberia up so to speak!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24020-mateus","name":"Mateus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24020_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T07:26:44-07:00","id":1221697,"title":"","content":"As the author of Beast!Baba Yaga - yes, she is stated as <b>Beast</b>'s Horror. In <b>Beast: the Primordial </b> term Horror means your atavistic, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1220337-astral-space-dreams-inspirations\">monstrous soul from Astral Realm</a>, not the fleshy Horrors of the <b>CoD Rulebook</b>. In the end they can end the same ( as end game of <b>Beast</b> ), but generally, Beast!Horror is much more akin to Ephemeral Beings possessing human. If you do not want to use <b>Beast</b> game as template, do what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar38_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"38\" data-vbnamecard=\"38\">Cinder</a> points you to. You can still use my Beast!Baba Yaga as collection of Condition that would be in here 'headquarter' - just use all the Tilts in Lair section of it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 05-24-2018, 11:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}